# AI Native Application Server

```text
Cliente -> Rust (API + backend tradicional)
              └─ use case agentic? -> Mojo (agentes, RAG, harness)
```

Rust is the only public process. Clients must never call Mojo directly.

## Process split

| Process | Path | Owns | Must not do |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Rust runtime | `runtime-rust/` | public HTTP, CRUD, DBs, auth, request control | agent graph, RAG, harness |
| Mojo agent engine | `src/` | agents, orchestration, RAG, retrieval, harness | public ingress, traditional CRUD |

Not every request uses Mojo. The agent engine stays in the repo even when dormant. A Rust use case invokes it only when the flow needs an agent.

Do not add Python to the Mojo process. Do not introduce `src/interop/python` or `src/python`.

## Mojo layers

| Layer | Path | Owns | Must not do |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Domain | `src/domain/` | types, rules, ports/traits | I/O, vendors |
| Application | `src/application/` | agent use cases, graph, RAG | public HTTP/JSON |
| Bootstrap | `src/bootstrap/` | composition root | business rules |
| Transport | `src/transport/` | internal HTTP + ACE1 | domain rules |
| Infrastructure | `src/infrastructure/` | sockets, env, local adapters | domain rules |

`src/ai_orchestrator/` is leftover FastAPI (Strangler). Do not extend it.

vLLM / LiteLLM stay as external HTTP services. Training/HF serving stay out of both processes.

## Placement rule

- Traditional backend feature → Rust, state the layer.
- Agent / RAG / harness feature → Mojo, state the layer.

```mojo
var tokenizer = Tokenizer()
var tokens = tokenizer.encode("Hello Mojo")
```
